# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# What a press on the view is stays its own until its button is up, on the
# demo block (application events only: a physical trackpad is checked by
# docs/macos-trackpad-checklist.md). Run by
# tools/ui-navigation-gesture-state-test.sh (Linux),
# tools/ui-windows-navigation-gesture-state-test.ps1 (Windows) and
# tools/ui-macos-navigation-test.sh (macOS), in the Floating and the Docked
# layout:
#   - mitcad#1571: Option pressed during a select keeps it a window
#     selection, Option released during an orbit keeps it an orbit and
#     picks nothing; Ctrl released during a click, then a one-pixel move,
#     is still a Ctrl click that adds the edge.
#   - mitcad#1572: a pan or orbit scroll while the button is held leaves
#     the press a click; a ScrollEnd with a delta lets the trackpad's button
#     up at once; the phases Qt makes of macOS's (resting fingers, Ended
#     with a delta, a momentum begun as a new scroll).
#   - mitcad#1573: the window deactivated during an F4, Option or scroll
#     drag ends it and the next click picks; a panel taking the keyboard
#     does not end it; F4 released after the keyboard went to a panel
#     leaves the next left click a pick (MiddlePanF4).
wait-idle
expect-viewport
expect-navigation-gesture-state
key Escape
expect-selection 0 0
capture-view-orientation picks
click-edge-release 1 modifier-first
expect-selection 1 0
click-edge-release 2 key-up-moved
expect-selection 2 0
expect-view-buttons none
expect-view-orientation ${picks} unchanged
key Escape
expect-selection 0 0
view-navigation middle-pan-f4
capture-view-orientation f4
click-edge-release 1 f4-elsewhere
expect-selection 1 0
expect-view-buttons none
expect-view-orientation ${f4} unchanged
view-navigation middle-pan
key Escape
expect-never '^(TestDriver: FAIL|OCCT view event failed)'
